{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>Under a servant</b> — whom HaShem has made king over them because of their sin, and he does not pity his ruler; the people tremble." "<b>And a fool</b> — when he is sated and rules, because of their transgression." "<b>And under a woman</b> — when she is married, for she hates those who hate her, because they despised her and did not contain her; therefore they fear. And it is possible that she was violated because of the sin of those who hate her." "<b>And a maidservant</b> — who is heiress to her mistress and rules over her because of the transgression of the mistress; therefore it is fitting for a man to guard against sin, that the lowly not rule over the honorable."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:25:38.867056937Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}